<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-169 Phase B, Gap 1 (bead nexus-zw2em) - retention TEXT NOT NULL
    DEFAULT 'full' CHECK (retention IN ('reference-only','full')) on
    nexus.chunks, plus ALTER COLUMN chunk_text DROP NOT NULL: the schema
    slice that lets a chunk row carry identity (address + span + chash +
    metadata + embedding) without content, for a reference-only consumer
    (Conductus / any docuverse client) that owns the bytes elsewhere.

    RE-TARGETED FROM chunks_&lt;dim&gt; TO nexus.chunks (session nexus-70,
    Sam: 'do it', 2026-09-11): RDR-169's own Technical Design section
    predates RDR-191 Phase 4 (vectors-004-unify-chunks.xml), which collapsed
    chunks_384/768/1024 into ONE nexus.chunks table with three nullable
    typed embedding columns (embedding_384/768/1024, exactly_one_embedding
    CHECK). Every "per chunks_&lt;dim&gt;" instruction in the RDR now applies
    to nexus.chunks alone - there is only one table to ALTER, not three.
    (RDR-169's cross-repo conexus etl_t3.py pairing is separately moot:
    conexus-od6a records the T3 ETL as the retired migration path, so this
    is engine-only with no paired client-repo edit - unlike memory-003's
    contemporaneous client pairing, which genuinely needed one.)

    chunk_tsv GENERATED EXPRESSION IS UNCHANGED (CA-2, verified by schema
    spike, RDR-169 Research Findings): nexus.chunks.chunk_tsv is
    `GENERATED ALWAYS AS (to_tsvector('english', chunk_text)) STORED` with
    no NOT NULL of its own (vectors-004-unify-chunks.xml). Postgres
    evaluates `to_tsvector('english', NULL)` to a NULL tsvector, which the
    `@@` match operator and the GIN index (idx_chunks_tsv) both treat as a
    non-match - a reference-only row is excluded from every FTS/hybrid
    candidate path (vectors-007's hybrid_search_&lt;dim&gt;: `chunk_tsv @@
    plainto_tsquery(...) OR p_query_text &lt;% chunk_text` - both operands
    NULL, both false) by construction, with zero edit to the generated
    column itself. The earlier COALESCE(chunk_text,'') idea (RDR-169
    Alternatives) is unnecessary: empty and NULL tsvector both exclude.

    embedding_384/768/1024 stay nullable-per-column / exactly_one_embedding
    CHECK unchanged (a reference-only chunk is still a vector - G4's
    embed-without-store route stores a caller-supplied precomputed
    embedding, never a NULL one); tenant_id stays NOT NULL (RDR-169 binding
    constraint 3: RLS is unconditional, content nullability is orthogonal
    to tenancy). RLS itself (ENABLE/FORCE + tenant_isolation policy,
    vectors-004 step 3) is untouched - this changeset is a bare ADD
    COLUMN + ALTER COLUMN, no DML, so the FORCE-RLS migration-role DML
    no-op class (nexus-1wjmq) does not apply here (see
    tests/test_changelog_rls_lint.py's own scope note: only DML against a
    FORCE table is in-scope for that lint).

    Re-index / retention-transition semantics (RDR-169 Technical Design):
    a full -> reference-only transition is PROHIBITED at the application
    layer (PgVectorRepository#upsertReferenceOnlyChunk's pre-INSERT guard
    SELECT, nexus-xvb6b) - not by a schema-level trigger/CHECK here. The
    schema only distinguishes "content present" (chunk_text NOT NULL,
    retention='full') from "content absent" (chunk_text NULL,
    retention='reference-only'); the invariant "chunk_text NOT NULL implies
    retention='full'" is an application contract the guard enforces, not
    something a CHECK across two columns encodes in this changeset (a
    two-column CHECK would also have to tolerate the legitimate transient
    ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE path where only embedding/metadata are refreshed
    - left to the app-layer guard, as designed).

    Placed after tuples-002-sweep-indexes.xml (current tail) and before the
    grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block, matching the established
    late-append convention (D0.1; see vectors-013's / memory-003's own
    &lt;include&gt; comments for the identical reasoning).

    D0.6 rollback: drops the CHECK and the column, restores chunk_text NOT
    NULL. A reference-only row (chunk_text NULL) cannot survive that
    restoration - stated inline, not silently omitted, matching
    memory-003-ttl-days.xml's identical rollback discipline: any
    reference-only row present at rollback time is UNREPRESENTABLE under
    the pre-migration shape and the ALTER COLUMN ... SET NOT NULL will
    fail loud (not silently coerce) if one exists. This is deliberate: a
    rollback that silently deleted or NULL-coerced live docuverse data
    would be worse than a rollback that refuses.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-014-1" author="nexus-zw2em">
        <comment>
            RDR-169 Phase B Gap 1: nexus.chunks gains retention TEXT NOT NULL
            DEFAULT 'full' CHECK (retention IN ('reference-only','full'));
            chunk_text DROP NOT NULL. chunk_tsv generated expression,
            exactly_one_embedding CHECK, tenant_id NOT NULL, and RLS are all
            unchanged (see file header).
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks
    ADD COLUMN retention TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'full'
    CONSTRAINT chunks_retention_chk CHECK (retention IN ('reference-only', 'full'));

ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks
    ALTER COLUMN chunk_text DROP NOT NULL;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks
    ALTER COLUMN chunk_text SET NOT NULL;

ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks
    DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS chunks_retention_chk;

ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks
    DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS retention;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
